yo yo what's up internet people this is  dr john delony with ramsey network  today we are talking about chemical  imbalances anxiety  and when should we take medication for  anxiety would that  fix us okay so i'm responding to an  email i got at ash john  ramseysolutions.com by the way i'm  getting emails from all over the country  tons of them keep them coming they're so  good and we're about to launch the john  dalone show in the next couple of months  so keep them coming i'm loving it okay  so this email is from  andrew hey dr d what's up i've heard  that anxiety can be caused by a chemical  imbalance in your body  is this true and does this require  medication to balance out  or will things like box breathing and  journaling help  long term to balance me out i have  extreme anxiety and it's only getting  worse  respectfully andrew number one  big time shout out to andrew for being  vulnerable being  open thank you for your note i'm getting  this question from  everybody i get it from my family  members from my co-workers from people i  meet in the grocery store  not really and especially from emails  so here's my thoughts on medication on  anxiety  and chemical imbalances is anxiety  caused by chemical imbalance in our  brain  i want to back away from that question  because i really don't like  the way that questions posed the short  answer is yes  all of our actions are electronic and  magnetic  and chemical based everything we do  going to the bathroom it's a chemical  imbalance um  being attracted to somebody it's a  chemical imbalance being angry it's a  chemical imbalance  feeling hungry it's a chemical  everything's a chemical imbalance  and so we often hear the word chemical  imbalance and we think  i'm broken and what needs to be fixed  is the chemical level in my head i'm  going to go with somebody and get an  external chemical and it's going to fix  my internal problem  it's going to level me out and all is  going to be well  it's not really how it works and we  could go into all the biochemistry and  all the hormones and all of the  histories and all the stuff  but instead i'm going to answer that  question pretty simply in a few short  steps  first i love how brene brown says it  genetics loads the gun  and environment pulls the trigger when  it comes to your psychology into your  brain chemistry  who you are genetically chemically  plays a role in the world you grew up in  also plays a role and you're not a  static robot your  genome your genes don't make you who  you're going to be  your genes can be turned on and off and  expressed and  unexpressed and muted because of all  sorts of different things  from the air you breathe the  relationships you have the relationships  you didn't have  trauma good nutrition all sorts of  different things  i also love the phrase that we throw  around in counseling a lot which is your  childhood biography becomes your adult  biology how much adrenaline and cortisol  were flowing through your veins as a kid  when you were trying to protect yourself  from  trauma when you're trying to connect  with a parent who is too busy texting  all of those things turn into your adult  wiring and the third thing is we can  control our thoughts  and our actions we can control  what we think about all the time and  it's hard and it's challenging  and depending on our genetic wiring and  depending on  some of our life histories depending on  some of the things that have happened to  us  our addictions our coping mechanisms the  things we do when we want to numb or  hide  controlling our thoughts is really hard  or when you're locked in your house for  five months because the world's shut  down because of some invisible virus  or you get laid off or you found out she  cheated on you again  or your grandmother passes away all  those things set off  different fire alarms and that's why i  say often anxiety is just a fire alarm  is it chemical yeah but it's  so much more than that so the question  andrew asks here is  does it require medication to fix  anxiety  the answer is usually no usually no  usually with the right relationships the  right exercise and nutrition program  the right meditating journaling  breathing being  present program which we call  life anxiety just is a normal ebb and  flow in your life  there are times like he mentions here he  has extreme anxiety  when i got laid low by anxiety just  wiped out  i spent a couple of years taking anxiety  medication and what  it does is it just silences the alarms  it's like going out to the back of your  house back behind the garage with a pair  of hedge clippers  where the electricity is coming in and  you just turn the power off to the  alarms  it just shuts them off it doesn't fix  you  it just shuts them off but when my  alarms were finally  quiet then i got to do the hard work of  uncovering childhood traumas  reforming and remaking relationships  learning how to journal learning how to  sit with a counselor  learning how to get to know myself for  the first time so in my world  they were really helpful for a short  period of time and i worked specifically  with a doctor  and when i met with my doctor for the  first time i said i will not put a pill  in my mouth until i have an exit  strategy  and we worked together to make sure that  worked out  and i'm happy to say i haven't taken  medication in years and years and years  and my anxiety alarms will go off  because they should  because it's a healthy important part of  our lives  but i also know when they're about to  take off when they're about to head for  the hills  when they're about to really start going  and i've got enough tools like box  breathing i've got enough tools like  calling a friend i've got enough tools  like  a community that's my emergency fund for  life  my spirituality my daily practices  my nutrition my exercise things that i  do on a regular basis  that keep the alarms from getting out of  control so if you're suffering from  extreme anxiety andrew  go talk to somebody you know you better  than anybody  and when you feel alone and you feel  like everyone around you is crazy  and when every time you open your eyes  your heart starts beating  and all you're doing is scrolling  through looking for the next  worst thing you will find the next worst  thing  that's the demon of anxiety so go find a  counselor  go find somebody to talk to and see if  medication is right for you go talk to a  doctor  i hope this helps andrew if you or  anybody else has  more questions about brain chemistry  anxiety depression  how that all works and you all want to  take a super deep dive hit me up at ask  john  ramseysolutions.com otherwise i will see  you soon  take care be kind to one another go  exercise eat good  and get a good night's sleep take care
 

